<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Android's own backup of the app's data, on Android 12 and later: on by
   the owner's choice (2026-10-20), said on Settings > Backup, and the
   person's to turn off there (2026-10-27): NotesBackupAgent then hands
   Android only a mark saying so, which replaces the copy made while on,
   and these rules are unused. With nothing included or
   excluded, all of the app's files go, the notebook among them, to the
   person's Google account when backup is on in the phone's settings,
   and to a new phone in a transfer; they come back when the app is
   installed again. Not past 25 MB of data, Android's limit, which the
   page says. The cache, where a shared PDF waits, is never part of it.
   The backup .zip is the copy a person keeps and moves; this one only
   restores the app. No encryption is required here
   (disableIfNoEncryptionCapabilities is not set), so nothing claims it.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup />
    <device-transfer />
</data-extraction-rules>
